::heading level=1 id=browser-check
Browser Render Check
::end

::paragraph id=browser-check-summary
What a browser has to get right for a `.dx` to be readable on github.com, and what holds each one. Resolution happens in the reader's own browser — `editor/github/resolve.js` decides what is shown, and `docs/github.md` says why it has to work that way.
::end

::html id=browser-check-table
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>What is checked</th><th>Held by</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td>Blob page</td><td>A pointer is replaced by the document it stands for.</td><td><code>resolve.test.mjs</code></td></tr>
		<tr><td>Diff page</td><td>A one-line digest change expands into a document diff.</td><td><code>resolve.test.mjs</code></td></tr>
		<tr><td>Engine</td><td>Every build renders the bytes <code>dx render</code> writes.</td><td><code>engine.test.mjs</code></td></tr>
		<tr><td>Markup</td><td>Author HTML and SVG pass an allow-list, never a deny-list.</td><td><code>render::escape</code></td></tr>
		<tr><td>Pack transfer</td><td>A pack is named in a call, and crosses once per revision.</td><td><code>engine.test.mjs</code></td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
::end

::heading level=2 id=browser-check-where-heading
Where the engine runs
::end

::paragraph id=browser-check-where
A content script inherits github.com's WebAssembly policy, and that policy does not let the engine compile. So the page does the fetching — only a page-context request carries the reader's session, which is what makes private repositories work — and the extension's own background context does the rendering.
::end

::svg id=browser-check-svg
<svg viewBox="0 0 720 200" role="img" aria-label="The page fetches the pack and asks the extension background context, which answers from dx serve when it is running and from bundled wasm when it is not">
	<g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.5">
		<rect x="1" y="20" width="170" height="44"/>
		<rect x="265" y="20" width="170" height="44"/>
		<rect x="550" y="1" width="169" height="38"/>
		<rect x="550" y="55" width="169" height="38"/>
		<path d="M171 42 L259 42"/>
		<path d="M251 36 L259 42 L251 48" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
		<path d="M435 42 L495 42 M495 42 L495 20 L544 20 M495 42 L495 74 L544 74"/>
		<path d="M536 14 L544 20 L536 26 M536 68 L544 74 L536 80" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
	</g>
	<g fill="currentColor" font-family="monospace" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">
		<text x="86" y="47">the page</text>
		<text x="350" y="47">background</text>
		<text x="634" y="25">dx serve</text>
		<text x="634" y="79">bundled wasm</text>
	</g>
	<g fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.55" font-family="monospace" font-size="11">
		<text x="0" y="88">fetches the pack with</text>
		<text x="0" y="104">the reader's own session</text>
		<text x="265" y="88">wasm may compile here,</text>
		<text x="265" y="104">and only here</text>
		<text x="550" y="116">whichever answers,</text>
		<text x="550" y="132">nothing can tell</text>
	</g>
	<line x1="0" y1="164" x2="720" y2="164" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.2"/>
	<text x="0" y="186" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.55" font-family="monospace" font-size="11">the pack is named in a call, never carried inside one</text>
</svg>
::end

::checklist id=browser-check-list
[x] Chrome, Firefox, and Safari each take the extension by their own route
[x] Blob, blame, commit, and pull-request pages all render
[x] No page shows a raw `~ dx1` line
[ ] Confirm a private repository in a signed-in browser
::end
